{
  "_meta": "Reviewed snapshot of English-identical locale values, adjudicated by Chris 2026-08-04: cognates, units/symbols, and product vocabulary are ACCEPTED; check-i18n section D flags any English-identical value NOT listed here (the ratchet). pending = provisionally tolerated awaiting a Chris ruling; move to accepted or fix, do not let entries rot here. (2026-08-04: the nl samples pair was RULED translate-not-accept -> \"metingen\"; pending is now empty.) (2026-08-14: metrics.unit_per_m2 / unit_per_min added under the units/symbols rule — the localizing locales ar/he/ru/ja/ko/tr/zh DO differ, which is the proof the values are real rather than untranslated.) (2026-08-14: metrics.unit_per_m2 / unit_per_min added under the units/symbols rule. ar/he/ru/ja/ko/tr/zh DO differ, which is the proof these are real values rather than untranslated ones — both were DERIVED from strings the locales already had, never authored.) (2026-08-14: setup.subtab_system accepted for de/pl under the COGNATE rule — 'System' is the ordinary German and Polish word, not an untranslated string; the other 15 locales do differ, which is the proof.) (2026-10-26: vocab.path_type.standard de/fr/it and vocab.dreame.fan_speed.turbo cs/de/fr/it/ja/nl added as REPLICAS of rulings already in this file, not as new adjudications — vocab.fan_speed.standard carries 'Standard' for exactly de/fr/it and vocab.fan_speed.max carries 'Max' for exactly those six locales, and the two new keys hold the identical English values ('Standard', 'Max') for the identical locale sets. Found because --strict-coverage, which docs/dev/frontend/i18n-system.md calls release-gate mode, was RED on these nine at 2.5.0 while the permissive run that gates a push was green; nothing runs the strict mode in CI.) (2026-10-27: SEVEN pairs REMOVED, reversing part of the 2026-08-04 product-vocabulary line and the whole of the 2026-10-26 replica note above. vocab.fan_speed.max, vocab.dreame.fan_speed.turbo and vocab.battery_bucket_key.max lose 'ja' -> all three now read 最大; theme_preview.shell.kicker loses 'ar' and 'ru' -> هيكل EVCC / Оболочка EVCC; vocab.token_type.easing loses 'he' -> האטה; theme_preview.foundations.chip loses 'zh-Hant' -> 標籤. The reason in every case is the SAME PACK CONTRADICTING ITSELF, not a judgement about the language: ja.json already renders Max as 最大 in room_rules.help_max / maintenance.interval_max_hint / saved_zones.over_cap; ar.json already renders this sense of Shell as هيكل in four theme_preview keys and ru.json as оболочка in four; he.json already renders easing as האטה in evcc_reorder_flip_easing and evcc_learning_anim_ease; zh-Hant.json already uses 標籤 for the chip component in theme_group.chips and six token rows. Found by a rule section D cannot express -- a NON-LATIN-SCRIPT locale whose value still carries a Latin word, placeholders and units stripped -- which returned 15 candidates: these 7, seven font.opendyslexic (a typeface name, correct), and ja common.ok (standard in Japanese UIs; note ru transliterates to ОК). INVARIANT THIS LEAVES BEHIND: all six of these entries now list Latin-script locales only. The rule's floor: it says nothing about the 817 of 898 accepted pairs that sit in Latin-script locales, where a cognate and an untranslated word are byte-identical to it.) (2026-10-27, census wave 1: THREE entries added, all REPLICAS of rulings already in this file rather than new adjudications. vocab.fan_speed.boost_iq and .boostiq are the two stored display spellings Eufy's FAN_SPEED_ALIASES accepts for the `boost` rung, and they are accepted for ALL locales ('*') because their value is the PRODUCT NAME 'BoostIQ', which Eufy's app shows untranslated in every language. That deliberately breaks the Latin-script-only invariant the 2026-10-27 note left behind, for the same reason font.opendyslexic does: it is a name, not a word. An earlier draft of this entry keyed both to 'Boost' and copied vocab.fan_speed.boost's de/id/nl ruling -- wrong, because that substitutes core's canonical word for the brand's own. vocab.water_level.auto is accepted for the eight Latin packs that use the same abbreviation; the other nine translate it (ja/zh 自動, ru Авто, tr Otomatik, ...), which is the proof it is a real abbreviation rather than an untranslated string. vocab.dreame.fan_speed.strong gains 'fr' only: 'intense' is an ordinary French word spelt identically, and the other 16 packs do differ, which is the proof. Checked the PARENT ruling rather than copying it blind, because an accepted-in-error entry is invisible to section D forever and a replica inherits the error.) (2026-10-27, census wave 6: SIX entries, 64 pairs, for the rule editor's card-local vocabularies. The four comparison operators are accepted for the FIFTEEN LTR packs and deliberately NOT for '*': ar and he carry WORDS ('أكبر من', 'גדול מ-') because a bare '>' is ambiguous in a right-to-left layout, and that difference is the whole reason those four have keys at all rather than staying hardcoded symbols. A mathematical symbol is the units/symbols rule, not untranslated text. room_rules.operator_group.existence (cs, fr) and room_rules.entity_category.text (cs, de) are the cognate rule; the other packs do differ, which is the proof.) (2026-10-27, census wave 7: SECTION E added, and `latin_in_non_latin` with it. Its residue over all 49,699 shipped values was TWO, both zh-Hant: theme.tab_tokens, left as 'Token' because en.js's own translator note on that key said \"jargon, keep as 'tokens'\" while zh-Hans/ja/ko/ru had translated it, an inconsistency against the note and not mine to settle; and external_jobs.empty_app_branded, '{brand} App', where 'App' is ordinary written Chinese in Taiwan. Section E reaches a case section D cannot: these are Latin-script but not English-IDENTICAL, so the ratchet never looked at them.) (2026-10-28: the first of those was SETTLED and theme.tab_tokens is gone from `latin_in_non_latin` — the note was the thing that was wrong, so zh-Hant now reads 令牌 and the section E residue is ONE. Also, `pending` is NOT empty, whatever the 2026-08-04 line above says: it was true that day, and then vocab.obstacle_type.cable [es] and .pedestal [es, pt] were parked on 2026-08-06 and are still awaiting a ruling. Read the `pending` object, never the prose here.)",
  "rationales": {
    "_note": "Per-entry rationales for full-phrase / sentence entries in `accepted`. The general rule (see _meta) is units/symbols/cognates only; anything longer needs a rationale here explaining why the Latin-locale packs deliberately keep the English form.",
    "metrics.battery_samples_tooltip": "Full explanatory sentence — an in-tooltip clarification of the samples/count ratio. The 10 Latin locales (cs/de/es/fr/id/it/nl/pl/pt/tr) all use the same English wording deliberately: the message is a tightly-worded methodological note that maps directly onto a domain term (\"sampled\") whose meaning does not survive loose paraphrase, and no shipping locale currently attempts it. Retranslate at any point without penalty; the accepted-list entry is provisional, not a design choice.",
    "rooms.override_order.*": "The 11 keys under this namespace are the sequence-toggle card row's UI copy (added in task 4, 89195039). Eight of the eleven values are full English phrases or sentences — 'Override device order', 'Vacuum optimises the path itself', 'Changes the saved sequence in your Roborock app' and the like. The Latin-locale packs (cs/de/es/fr/id/it/nl/pl/pt/tr) hold them in English pending a translator's pass on a stable release, because (a) the feature is Roborock V1 only and its user base is small, and (b) translating the imperative 'Override' and the participle 'optimises' out of English is easy to get wrong in a way that misleads about consent — the copy is load-bearing (window.confirm on Clear reads to a user's mental model). Retranslate when a translator can review the full flow."
  },
