  "latin_in_non_latin": {
    "_note": "Section E only. A value that is ENTIRELY LATIN SCRIPT in a non-Latin pack and is correct that way. Separate from `accepted` on purpose: these are not English-IDENTICAL, so section D never sees them, and filing them under `accepted` would claim something untrue. `theme.tab_tokens` was removed 2026-10-28 on Chris's ruling that tokens SHOULD translate: it is a visible sub-tab label, and zh-Hant was the only pack still following the translator note. Measured across the packs rather than estimated — twelve translate it or decline it in their own spelling, four (de/es/nl/pt) keep \"Tokens\" as a loanword and are listed under `accepted`. An earlier version of this note said \"16 of 17 packs already translated it\", which counted the loanword four as translations. zh-Hant now reads 令牌. The remaining entry is a proper noun inside an app-branded empty state, which no pack should translate.",
    "external_jobs.empty_app_branded": [
      "zh-Hant"
    ]
  },
